module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.SubmoduleOpen
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.Algebra

/-!
# Graded ideals of a sheaf-level graded algebra, and the one generated in a single degree

Situation 01NN fixes a scheme `S` together with a quasi-coherent, commutative, nonnegatively
graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜`, in the sheaf-level form
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra`. This file introduces the graded
ideals of such an algebra and constructs the one that a submodule `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` of a single
homogeneous piece generates: the degreewise family `(ℱ𝒜)_n`, smallest among the families of
`𝒪_S`-submodules with local membership containing every product `f · a` of a local section `f` of
`ℱ` with a local section `a` of `𝒜` in the complementary degree.

This is the algebra-side input of Tags 0801 and 0802, both of whose statements name a quotient
`𝒜/ℐ` of a sheaf-level graded algebra by a graded ideal. The quotient itself is not constructed in
this file; see the section "Related declarations" below.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.GradedIdeal`: a graded ideal of a sheaf-level
  graded algebra — an `𝒪_S`-submodule of each homogeneous piece, stable under multiplication by
  arbitrary homogeneous local sections of the algebra.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.IsGeneratedInDegree`: the property of a
  submodule of `𝒜_n` of containing every product `f · a` with `f` a local section of `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d`
  and `a` a local section of `𝒜_m`, for `d + m = n`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.generatedByDegree`: the degree-`n` piece
  `(ℱ𝒜)_n` of the graded ideal generated by `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d`, the infimum of the submodules with that
  property.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mulStabilizerSubmodule` and
  `mulStabilizer`: the auxiliary submodule of `𝒜_i` through which multiplicative stability of
  `ℱ𝒜` is proved.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree`: **the graded
  ideal sheaf `ℱ𝒜` generated by a submodule in one degree**, i.e. `generatedByDegree` packaged
  with its stability under multiplication.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.isGeneratedInDegree_generatedByDegree`:
  `(ℱ𝒜)_n` does contain the generators, so the infimum defining it is attained and every
  statement proved from `IsGeneratedInDegree` applies to it.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.generatedByDegree_le`: `(ℱ𝒜)_n` is the
  *smallest* such submodule, which is the universal property the generation rests on.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mul_mem_generatedByDegree`: **`ℱ𝒜` is an
  ideal.** The product of a local section of `(ℱ𝒜)_i` with an arbitrary homogeneous local
  section of `𝒜` of degree `j` lies in `(ℱ𝒜)_(i + j)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.le_generatedByDegree_self`: `ℱ` itself is
  contained in `(ℱ𝒜)_d`, so the generation loses nothing.

## Implementation notes

**Why submodules and not subsheaves.** Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.Submodule M` is a submodule of
the underlying presheaf of modules whose membership condition is local, with
`SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSheafOfModules` realising it as an honest sheaf of modules and
`SheafOfModules.Submodule.ι` as a monomorphism into `M`. That is the notion of an ideal sheaf
Tags 0801 and 0802 use, and it carries the `CompleteLattice` instance
`SheafOfModules.Submodule.instCompleteLattice` (Tag 01AP), which is what lets the generated ideal
be an infimum instead of a sheafification: the infimum of submodules with local membership is the
sheafification of the sectionwise span, so no sheafification has to be performed by hand. The
construction mirrors `Stacks.IdealPowerSheaf.idealPow`, the powers of an ideal subsheaf of a
structure sheaf, which is the infimum of the submodules containing the relevant products and
whose product law is proved the same way; the difference is that the family here is indexed by
the degrees of a graded algebra rather than by an exponent, so the ambient sheaf changes with the
index and the product law changes degree.

The infimum is taken over a subtype rather than written as `sInf` of a set, so that membership is
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_iInf_submodule_obj` applied once.

**The `Scheme.Modules` type synonym.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` for
`SheafOfModules S.ringCatSheaf` with its own category instance, so neither dot notation nor
instance search reaches through it: `CompleteLattice (SheafOfModules.Submodule (𝒜.piece n))` is
not found for a piece of a `SheafGradedAlgebra`, whose type is `S.Modules`. The file therefore
declares `attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`; no alias and no
second lattice instance is introduced.

**Degrees, and why `HEq` and not a cast.** The product of sections of degrees `d` and `m` lives in
`𝒜_(d + m)`, while the degree-`n` piece of the generated ideal is about sections of `𝒜_n`; the two
agree only propositionally. Following the `mul_assoc`, `mul_one` and `mul_comm` fields of
`SheafGradedAlgebra` itself, the relation is recorded as a heterogeneous equality with the degree
equation `d + m = n` carried as a separate hypothesis. The hypothesis is what makes the
heterogeneous equality usable rather than decorative: `subst` on it identifies the two types,
after which `eq_of_heq` applies and the rest of the proof is ordinary rewriting. A transport
`h ▸ _` in place of the `HEq` would put a cast inside every consumer.

**Where the sheaf condition is used.** Exactly once, in `mulStabilizer`. Multiplicative stability
is not provable directly from the infimum, because the defining condition of a member of it says
nothing about products of its own sections; so the auxiliary `mulStabilizer` is exhibited, whose
sections over `U` are the sections `x` of `𝒜_i` all of whose restrictions multiply `𝒜_j` into
`(ℱ𝒜)_(i + j)` for every `j`, and `(ℱ𝒜)_i` is below it by minimality. The quantification over all
smaller opens is what makes `mulStabilizer` stable under restriction, and locality of its
membership reduces to locality of `(ℱ𝒜)_(i + j)` through the pointwise description of the
covering sieves of `CategoryTheory.Opens.grothendieckTopology`: a sieve covers `U` exactly when
every point of `U` lies in the domain of one of its arrows. No finite-union bookkeeping is needed,
and the two covers are combined by intersecting opens.

**Two private helpers.** `resRes` and `resSelf`, that a double restriction is a single one and
that restriction along the identity is the identity, are `private` and used only inside proofs
here.

## Related declarations

No Stacks tag is attached in this file. The Stacks project introduces the graded ideal sheaf and
the quotient `𝒜/ℐ` inline, inside the statements of Tags 0801 and 0802 and the proof of Tag 07ZI;
it has no tag of its own, and neither 0801 nor 0802 is proved here.

The declarations below are in the namespace `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal`.

* The degreewise quotient `𝒜/ℐ` is `quotPiece`, formed at the level of presheaves, where it is
  sectionwise, and sheafified degreewise; it uses no tensor product.
* Quasi-coherence of `(ℱ𝒜)_n`, for every degree and any quasi-coherent `ℱ`, is
  `isQuasicoherent_generatedByDegree_of_mulFamily`, and
  `isQuasicoherentQuotPieces_gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree` discharges the hypothesis
  `IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces` of the quotient construction for `ℱ𝒜`. Since the degree equation
  `d + m = n` of `IsGeneratedInDegree` determines `m`, `(ℱ𝒜)_n` is the smallest submodule with
  local membership containing the products `f · a` with `f` a local section of `ℱ` and `a` one
  of `𝒜_(n - d)`; it is not the image of a morphism of modules,
  multiplication being a map on sections, so `AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasicoherent_imageSubmodule`
  does not apply, and the proof goes through the compatible family of spans over affine opens,
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.sheafSubmodule`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0802](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0802)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

universe u

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A graded ideal of a sheaf-level graded `𝒪_S`-algebra: an `𝒪_S`-submodule of each homogeneous
piece, stable under multiplication by an arbitrary homogeneous local section of the algebra. -/
public structure GradedIdeal (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) where
  /-- The submodule of the degree-`n` homogeneous piece. -/
  piece (n : ℤ) : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule
  /-- Multiplying a local section of the ideal by an arbitrary homogeneous local section of the
  algebra stays in the ideal, in the degree obtained by adding the two degrees. -/
  mul_mem (i j : ℤ) (U : S.Opens) {x : Γ(𝒜.piece i, U)}
    (hx : x ∈ (piece i).toSubmodule.obj (op U)) (b : Γ(𝒜.piece j, U)) :
    (𝒜.mul i j).app U x b ∈ (piece (i + j)).toSubmodule.obj (op U)

variable (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) {d : ℤ} (ℱ : (𝒜.piece d).Submodule)

/-- The property, of a submodule `N` of the degree-`n` piece of `𝒜`, of containing every product
`f · a` of a local section `f` of `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` with a local section `a` of `𝒜_m`, whenever
`d + m = n`.

The degree equation is carried as a hypothesis and the product is related to the section of `𝒜_n`
by a heterogeneous equality, exactly as in the `mul_assoc` field of `SheafGradedAlgebra`;
substituting the equation identifies the two types and turns the `HEq` into an `Eq`. -/
public def IsGeneratedInDegree (n : ℤ) (N : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ (m : ℤ), d + m = n → ∀ (U : S.Opens) (f : Γ(𝒜.piece d, U)),
    f ∈ ℱ.toSubmodule.obj (op U) → ∀ (a : Γ(𝒜.piece m, U)) (x : Γ(𝒜.piece n, U)),
      HEq x ((𝒜.mul d m).app U f a) → x ∈ N.toSubmodule.obj (op U)

/-- The degree-`n` piece `(ℱ𝒜)_n` of the graded ideal generated by a submodule `ℱ` of the
degree-`d` piece: the smallest `𝒪_S`-submodule of `𝒜_n` with local membership containing every
product of a local section of `ℱ` with a homogeneous local section of `𝒜` of complementary
degree. -/
public noncomputable def generatedByDegree (n : ℤ) : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule :=
  ⨅ N : {N : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule // IsGeneratedInDegree 𝒜 ℱ n N}, N.1

/-- `(ℱ𝒜)_n` is below every submodule containing the generators: the universal property of the
generated ideal, and the only way membership in it is ever used. -/
public theorem generatedByDegree_le {n : ℤ} {N : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule}
    (hN : IsGeneratedInDegree 𝒜 ℱ n N) : generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ n ≤ N :=
  iInf_le (fun N : {N : (𝒜.piece n).Submodule // IsGeneratedInDegree 𝒜 ℱ n N} => N.1) ⟨N, hN⟩

/-- **`(ℱ𝒜)_n` contains the generators.** The infimum defining it is therefore attained, and
every statement proved from `IsGeneratedInDegree` applies to it. -/
public theorem isGeneratedInDegree_generatedByDegree (n : ℤ) :
    IsGeneratedInDegree 𝒜 ℱ n (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ n) := by
  intro m hm U f hf a x hx
  exact (AlgebraicGeometry.mem_iInf_submodule_obj _ (op U) x).2
    (fun N => N.2 m hm U f hf a x hx)

/-- `ℱ` is contained in the degree-`d` piece of the ideal it generates, so the generation loses
nothing: a local section `f` of `ℱ` is the product of itself with the unit of `𝒜`. -/
public theorem le_generatedByDegree_self : ℱ ≤ generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ d := by
  intro X f hf
  exact isGeneratedInDegree_generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ d 0 (add_zero d) X.unop f hf (𝒜.one X.unop) f
    (𝒜.mul_one d X.unop f).symm

section MulStabilizer

variable {i : ℤ}

/-- The sections of `𝒜_i` over `U` all of whose restrictions multiply every homogeneous local
section of `𝒜` into the generated ideal, as an `𝒪_S(U)`-submodule.

The quantification over every smaller open `V` is what makes the family stable under
restriction. -/
public noncomputable def mulStabilizerSubmodule (U : S.Opens) :
    Submodule Γ(S, U) Γ(𝒜.piece i, U) where
  carrier := {x | ∀ (V : S.Opens) (h : V ≤ U) (j : ℤ) (b : Γ(𝒜.piece j, V)),
    (𝒜.mul i j).app V ((𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x) b ∈
      (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (i + j)).toSubmodule.obj (op V) }
  add_mem' := by
    intro x y hx hy V h j b
    have hres : (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (x + y) =
        (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x +
          (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op y := map_add _ _ _
    rw [hres, map_add, AddMonoidHom.add_apply]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ (hx V h j b) (hy V h j b)
  zero_mem' := by
    intro V h j b
    have hres : (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (0 : Γ(𝒜.piece i, U)) = 0 := map_zero _
    rw [hres, map_zero, AddMonoidHom.zero_apply]
    exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  smul_mem' := by
    intro c x hx V h j b
    have hres : (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (c • x) =
        S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op c • (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x :=
      Scheme.Modules.map_smul _ (homOfLE h) c x
    rw [hres, (𝒜.mul i j).map_smul_left]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hx V h j b)

/-- Restriction maps of the underlying abelian presheaf of a module on a scheme compose:
restricting `A → B → C` equals the direct restriction `A → C`. -/
private theorem resRes (M : S.Modules) {A B C : S.Opens} (hBA : B ≤ A) (hCB : C ≤ B)
    (hCA : C ≤ A) (x : Γ(M, A)) :
    M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCB).op (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBA).op x) =
      M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCA).op x := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp]
  rfl

/-- Restricting a section along the identity inclusion leaves it unchanged. -/
private theorem resSelf (M : S.Modules) {U : S.Opens} (h : U ≤ U) (x : Γ(M, U)) :
    M.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x = x := by
  rw [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE h).op (𝟙 (op U)), M.presheaf.map_id]
  rfl

/-- The auxiliary submodule through which multiplicative stability of `ℱ𝒜` is proved: it is shown
below to contain the generators, hence to lie above `(ℱ𝒜)_i`, and its own definition makes the
desired products land in the ideal. -/
public noncomputable def mulStabilizer : (𝒜.piece i).Submodule where
  obj X := mulStabilizerSubmodule 𝒜 ℱ X.unop
  map := by
    intro X Y f x hx
    have hcast : ((𝒜.piece i).val.restrictₛₗ f) x =
        (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE (leOfHom f.unop)).op x := rfl
    intro V h j b
    rw [hcast, resRes (𝒜.piece i) (leOfHom f.unop) h (h.trans (leOfHom f.unop)) x]
    exact hx V (h.trans (leOfHom f.unop)) j b
  isSheaf := by
    intro X x hx V h j b
    refine (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (i + j)).isSheaf _ fun p hp => ?_
    obtain ⟨W, g, hxW, hpW⟩ := hx p (h hp)
    have hxW' : (𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE (leOfHom g)).op x ∈
        mulStabilizerSubmodule 𝒜 ℱ (i := i) W := hxW
    have hmem := hxW' (V ⊓ W) inf_le_right j
      ((𝒜.piece j).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := W))).op b)
    rw [resRes (𝒜.piece i) (leOfHom g) (inf_le_right (a := V) (b := W))
      (inf_le_right.trans (leOfHom g)) x] at hmem
    have hgoal : (𝒜.piece (i + j)).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := W))).op
        ((𝒜.mul i j).app V ((𝒜.piece i).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x) b) ∈
        (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (i + j)).toSubmodule.obj (op (V ⊓ W)) := by
      rw [(𝒜.mul i j).naturality (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := W)),
        resRes (𝒜.piece i) h (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := W))
          (inf_le_right.trans (leOfHom g)) x]
      exact hmem
    exact ⟨V ⊓ W, homOfLE inf_le_left, hgoal, hp, hpW⟩

/-- The generated ideal lies in the auxiliary submodule, because the auxiliary submodule contains
the generators: a product `(f · a) · b` is regrouped as `f · (a · b)` by associativity of `𝒜`, so
it is again a generator, in the degree obtained by adding the three degrees. -/
public theorem generatedByDegree_le_mulStabilizer :
    generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ i ≤ mulStabilizer 𝒜 ℱ (i := i) := by
  refine generatedByDegree_le 𝒜 ℱ ?_
  rintro m rfl U f hf a x hx
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hx
  intro V h j b
  refine isGeneratedInDegree_generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (d + m + j) (m + j) (add_assoc d m j).symm V
    ((𝒜.piece d).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f) (ℱ.toSubmodule.map_mem _ hf)
    ((𝒜.mul m j).app V ((𝒜.piece m).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a) b) _ ?_
  rw [(𝒜.mul d m).naturality h]
  exact 𝒜.mul_assoc d m j V _ _ b

end MulStabilizer

/-- **`ℱ𝒜` is an ideal.** The product of a local section of `(ℱ𝒜)_i` with an arbitrary
homogeneous local section of `𝒜` of degree `j` lies in `(ℱ𝒜)_(i + j)`. -/
public theorem mul_mem_generatedByDegree (i j : ℤ) (U : S.Opens) {x : Γ(𝒜.piece i, U)}
    (hx : x ∈ (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ i).toSubmodule.obj (op U)) (b : Γ(𝒜.piece j, U)) :
    (𝒜.mul i j).app U x b ∈ (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (i + j)).toSubmodule.obj (op U) := by
  have hx' := generatedByDegree_le_mulStabilizer 𝒜 ℱ (op U) hx U le_rfl j b
  rwa [resSelf (𝒜.piece i) le_rfl x] at hx'

/-- **The graded ideal sheaf generated by a submodule in one degree.** Given a sheaf-level graded
`𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜` and an `𝒪_S`-submodule `ℱ` of its degree-`d` homogeneous piece, this is the
graded ideal `ℱ𝒜`, with degree-`n` piece `(ℱ𝒜)_n`. -/
public noncomputable def gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree : GradedIdeal 𝒜 where
  piece n := generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ n
  mul_mem i j U := mul_mem_generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ i j U

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

end
